## eb9bdce4  (2026-05-01)

Initial recipe addition — GRPO on MAI-UI-2B (Tongyi-MAI's GUI-specialized 2B variant of the Qwen3-VL family). Two campaign variants:

- `run_0` — pure GRPO from base, no SFT step
- `run_1_sft_grpo` — SFT 2 epochs from 8B-teacher trajectories (reused from qwen3_vl_2b run_0) then GRPO 20 iters

Both target the same 86-task `complexity ≤ 2.0` train/eval pool used by qwen3_vl_2b / qwen3_5_2b on this env. Container is shared with qwen3_vl (same architecture / `transformers<5.0`).

Two stability patches applied this commit (after observing repeated `ActorUnavailableError` crashes across run_1 attempts 1-4):

- `scripts/train/utils/ray.sh` — `RAY_grpc_client_idle_timeout_ms=1800000` plus `RAY_health_check_*` and `RAY_core_worker_rpc_server_reconnect_timeout_max_s=1200`. Bumps ray's client-side gRPC channel idle threshold from ≈5 min to 30 min, covering the worst-case GIL-block window during which RolloutManager can't service health pings (caused by adb-daemon hangs across 32 parallel emulators).
- `lite/gym/envs/androidworld/main.py` — monkey-patches `android_env.AdbController.execute_command` to cap subprocess timeout at 30 s (default 120 s). Mitigates worst-case hung-adb propagation; secondary to the ray.sh fix.

run_1 attempt 5 with both patches active reached iter_19 in 4 h 21 m vs attempts 1-4 crashing in 1-2 h.
